From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] QVTKRenderWindowAdapter: set the blit target's draw buffer
 through vtkOpenGLState

QVTKRenderWindowAdapter::blit bound the target framebuffer and chose its
draw buffer with Qt's OpenGL functions, outside vtkOpenGLState.  For the
right eye of a quad-buffered window (QVTKOpenGLWindow with Crystal Eyes
stereo) that draw buffer is GL_BACK_RIGHT, while the cache still held the
GL_BACK it read when paintGL reset it; the first state check of
BlitDisplayFramebuffer then printed "Error in cache state for
GL_DRAW_BUFFER got 1027 expected1029" (GL_BACK_RIGHT, GL_BACK) at every
frame.  The left eye passed only because the check counts GL_BACK_LEFT as
GL_BACK.  ParaView shows these warnings in its Output Messages window
(ParaView issue 19038).

Bind the target and set its draw buffer through vtkOpenGLState, as the
same function already disables the scissor test through it, and as
QVTKOpenGLNativeWidget's blit moved to the state object in 2018 (VTK merge
request 4818).  The state object makes the GL calls when its cache
differs, and keeps the draw buffer of every stacked entry of that
framebuffer, so the Pop at the end of paintGL leaves the cache as OpenGL
has it.

Bug: https://gitlab.kitware.com/paraview/paraview/-/issues/19038
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/GUISupport/Qt/QVTKRenderWindowAdapter.cxx
+++ b/GUISupport/Qt/QVTKRenderWindowAdapter.cxx
@@ -311,9 +311,13 @@
       return false;
     }
 
-    f->glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, targetId);
-    const GLenum bufs[1] = { static_cast<GLenum>(targetAttachment) };
-    f->glDrawBuffers(1, bufs);
+    // Bind the target and select its draw buffer through vtkOpenGLState, as the
+    // scissor test below is, so that its cache follows what OpenGL draws to.
+    // Set directly, the right eye's GL_BACK_RIGHT left the cache at GL_BACK, and
+    // every state check of the blit that follows reported it.
+    auto ostate = this->RenderWindow->GetState();
+    ostate->vtkglBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, targetId);
+    ostate->vtkglDrawBuffer(static_cast<unsigned int>(targetAttachment));
 
     GLboolean scissorTest = f->glIsEnabled(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
     if (scissorTest == GL_TRUE)
